<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47958" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tesserŭla</span></b> , ae, f.
		dim.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				little</i> tessera. * </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A square bit of stone</i> for paving, Lucil. ap.
				<i><span class="en">Cic.
				Or. 44, 149</span></i>.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A votingtablet</i>, = <i>a
			ballot</i>, <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 3, 5, 18</span></i>.—
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A small tally</i> or <i>counter</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Gell. 10, 27, 5</span></i>.—Esp., <i>a ticket</i> for the distribution of corn, <i><span class="en">Pers. 5,
			74</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>IV.</b>
			<i>A die</i> used in play, <i><span class="en">Gell. 18,
				13, 2</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
